From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:03:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 180/182] hjviewer: review fixes for the privacy-mode end in
 the PC's incoming list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The privacy-mode fix ("a refused privacy-mode request leaves another
controller's privacy mode on") ends the PC's other remote screen
connections with on_close reason "privacy mode". The incoming history
(hjviewer_incoming.rs end_of) knew every other literal reason but not
this one, so it fell through to "lost": the PC's list said
"연결이 끊어짐" for a session the PC ended itself, and continued_by()
took a quick reconnect of that controller as a reconnect of the old row
("다시 연결 1번"), which hid why the session ended.

"privacy mode" now has its own end code "privacy" (in ENDS, so a stored
line keeps it), labelled "다른 연결이 개인정보 보호 모드를 켜서 끊김" /
"Ended: privacy mode turned on by another connection". It is not "lost",
so a reconnect starts a row of its own. Tests: the reason's end code,
the fold keeping a privacy end apart from a reconnect, the label in
both languages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
